# component: breadcrumb
# decisions: A11Y-2, API-16, DOC-1, DOC-2
# hunks:
#   A11Y-2: `BreadcrumbLink` gains `relative after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:-inset-y-1
#     after:content-['']`. Its visible box is one line of 14px text — measured 20px tall by the
#     geometry lane, 4px under the floor — and a breadcrumb is a ROW of navigation controls, not
#     prose, so SC 2.5.8's inline-text exception does not reach it. The invisible area grows the
#     pointer target on the block axis only, never the inline axis, so two adjacent crumbs cannot
#     fight for a pixel. Nothing moves and nothing paints. The ellipsis is untouched: it is
#     `role="presentation" aria-hidden` and upstream's own Collapsed example wraps it in a
#     `Button size="icon-sm"` that is already 32px — `breadcrumb.test.tsx` asserts that shape, so
#     a future upstream that makes the ellipsis itself the control fails here.
#   Nothing else. Upstream's breadcrumb paints no focus glow, sets no cursor and disables no
#     pointer events.
#   API-16: `"use client"` is ADDED. Upstream ships none, and `BreadcrumbLink` calls
#     `useRender` from `@base-ui/react/use-render`, which calls `React.useRef` internally — under
#     the `react-server` condition that hook is `undefined`, so a server component rendering a
#     breadcrumb link throws. `tooling/verify-rsc-safety.mjs` is what found it. API-16 puts the
#     boundary at the lowest interactive leaf, and this file is it.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
